>Roux</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Vertebral dimensions as risk factor of vertebral fracture in osteoporotic patients: a systematic literature review.</article-title><source>Osteoporos Int</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>1271</fpage><lpage>1278</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17340217</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Gilsanz2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilsanz</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Boechat</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Roe</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Loro</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Sayre</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Gender differences in vertebral body sizes in children and adolescents.</article-title><source>Radiology</source><volume>190</volume><fpage>673</fpage><lpage>677</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8115609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Duan1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Duan</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Turner</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>BT</given-names></name><name><surname>Seeman</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Sexual dimorphism in vertebral fragility is more the result of gender differences in age-related bone gain than bone loss.</article-title><source>J Bone Miner Res</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>2267</fpage><lpage>2275</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11760841</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Gilliam1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gilliam</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Freedson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Geenen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Shahraray</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Physical activity patterns determined by heart rate monitoring in 6&#x02013;7 year-old children.</article-title><source>Medicine &#x00026; Science in Sports &#x00026; Exercise</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>65</fpage><lpage>67</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7219138</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Taylor1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Twomey</surname><given-names>LT</given-names></name><name><surname>Corker</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><article-title>Bone and soft tissue injuries in post-mortem lumbar spines.</article-title><source>Paraplegia</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>129</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2235021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Seeman2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Seeman</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Pathogenesis of bone fragility in women and men.</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>359</volume><fpage>1841</fpage><lpage>1850</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12044392</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004836-Mosekilde1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mosekilde</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Sex differences in age-related loss of vertebral trabecular bone mass and structure&#x02013;biomechanical consequences.</article-title><source>Bone</source><vo